 :user-intent
 {:receipt-source "Independent immutable files built/admitted with Clio; causal IDs, not file order or filenames, connect the history."
  :assembly "receipts.edn can be assembled from the source segments; it must not remain the concurrent write hotspot."
  :fork-tax "Fork tax itself should be an EDN event ledger. Existing handoff documents should become generated artifacts with versioned names."
  :storage-options "Keep Git-resident events and Git-resident resource references as options; investigate Axxium references without assuming an installed durable content service."
  :preservation-scope "Preserve checkout-local work outside the orchestrator's active worktrees. Do not absorb, migrate, reset or rewrite that in-flight work."
  :quotes ["As long as the causal IDs are all present and we are building them with clio, they can be split up into as many files as we want."
           "This fork tax was to get anything we have right here that isn't a part of that persisted."
           "we want the fork tax documents we have been using, to be generated artifacts, with versioned names."]}
 :provisional-contract
 {:source-of-truth "Clio-admitted immutable events, with published schema identities and complete resolvable causal references; physical partitioning is a storage concern."
  :concurrent-writers "Allocate a unique process/run stream, preserving Clio stream/sequence laws. A branch or agent name alone is not a unique writer. No shared append file or unstated shared sequence allocator."
  :assembly "Use Clio's existing canonicalization and validation, not a second replay/identity engine in Foresight. File enumeration order and repartitioning must not change the admitted event set or canonical projection."
  :conflicts "Reject missing causes, cycles, inconsistent reuse of event IDs, stream/sequence collisions and unadmitted schemas through the owning Clio APIs. A partial union is incomplete, never a successful complete replay."
  :compatibility "Do not create the .ημ/receipts/ migration marker or freeze/split any existing ledger until its actual readers, writers and gates adopt the same source-selection contract. Preserve historical bytes and provenance."
  :snapshot-scope "Inventory explicit repository/path ownership and orchestration leases first. Report every item as selected, already recoverable with exact proof, protected active work, secret/private, or blocked/unclassified. Unclassified is not silently excluded or committed."
  :fork-tax-events "Model intent, scope selection, verification and publication outcomes as causal events using the existing owner seams. A planned push is not observed remote durability."
  :finite-snapshot "Pin a finite event/input selection before rendering. Publication acknowledgements may follow in separate immutable events; do not require a commit to contain its own hash or manufacture an endless bookkeeping chain."
  :generated-artifacts "Versioned names bind snapshot ID and projection revision/digest; render from pinned event/schema/renderer inputs, include selection identity and verification outcomes, never hand-edit reports as authority. A latest alias, if offered, is only a disposable pointer."
  :storage "Optional resource references retain immutable identity, exact content digest/size, access policy and retrieval/retention proof. Never equate a URL or authorization handle with durable recoverable bytes. No offloading or deletion in this turn."}
 :non-goals ["Implement a new Clio engine, Rheos parser or resource-store authority in Foresight."
             "Repair the existing receipt Git-buffer defect in parallel with its active worktrees."
             "Mass-convert ledgers, change active skill behavior, install a service or upload private material."
             "Claim the previous snapshot preserved uncommitted child content."
             "Treat local ultra review as native provider approval, PR merge permission or migration activation."]
