 :acceptance
 ["Permutation and repartition properties: the same admitted event set yields the same canonical replay and projection digest regardless of file enumeration or line grouping."
  "Concurrent same-agent/same-branch runs write distinct immutable files and streams, then union without collisions or a shared append hotspot."
  "Clio rejects inconsistent duplicate IDs, stream-slot collisions, gaps, missing predecessors/causes, cycles and unadmitted schemas; exact duplicate event copies follow Clio idempotency rather than being confused with conflicting IDs."
  "A source manifest identifies the complete selected input set and schemas; missing selected partitions or unresolved remote content cannot masquerade as a complete successful replay."
  "Publish a lossless bijection/mapping for legacy admission, preserve committed source bytes, reconcile active/excluded source declarations and qualify every writer/reader before cutover. The frozen old path and generated receipts.edn must not ambiguously share authority."
  "Pin renderer revision, schema identities and finite source/event selection. Regeneration emits byte-identical versioned artifacts; corrections and later publication observations are new events/projections, not edits to history."
  "Fork-tax publication records bind actual commit/tag/remote readback and exact selected bytes; report protected/unknown/private/residual content without claiming it persisted. Snapshot is not approval, installation or deployment."
  "Resource-reference mode remains optional; missing grants, digest mismatches, retention gaps and failed restore deny durable-preservation claims without deleting local content."
  "Test the actual adopted owner APIs and root CI path, including concurrent writers and interrupted publication; passing standalone fixtures alone does not activate migration."]
